      "text": "Diagram titled \"Bundling executable scripts\". pdf/forms.md on the left, pdf/extract_fields.py on the right, with an arrow from the highlighted `./extract_fields.py` link in the prose to the script itself. The script imports PdfReader from pypdf and defines write_field_info, which reads a PDF's form fields and writes them to JSON, with a __main__ guard checking argv length. The point is that a skill can bundle runnable code, not only prose.",
